.TH CHM-RUN-BINARY 1
.SH NAME
chm-run-binary \- inspect and explicitly launch supported executable formats
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 tools/run-compatible-binary.py
.I FILE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects ELF, PE/COFF, Mach-O, DOS MZ and WebAssembly headers before choosing a runtime.
Inspection is the default and does not execute the input. Use --run to execute or --dry-run
to display the selected runtime command. The tool reports native, QEMU, Wine, DOSBox,
Wasmtime or Wasmer execution mode explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --run
Execute the binary using the selected runtime.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the runtime and command without executing.
.TP
.B --sysroot DIR
Pass a Linux sysroot to QEMU user mode.
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Set execution timeout (default 60).
.TP
.B --json
Print header metadata as JSON during inspection.
.SH SAFETY
Only run trusted binaries. This tool does not provide a sandbox and does not download
or bypass signature checks for third-party executables. Use a disposable VM/container
for untrusted files. macOS binaries are not run on Linux merely by translating CPU
instructions because macOS system libraries and kernel interfaces are also required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 69 when no reviewed runtime is available; 124 on timeout.
